-- schema: project v1
-- Compactions as the releases rebuild them: 1.4.2 cuts everything
-- before the compaction's request; 1.14.30, before 1.14.40 was
-- released, keeps a tail before it; 1.18.0 moves that tail after the
-- summary; a session 1.10.0 created and a later release compacted
-- with a tail after 1.14.40's release; from 1.15.0, a compaction whose
-- summary failed but wrote a tail, which still cuts; and a tail that
-- starts at an assistant message, as splitTurn may choose. 1.4.2's
-- also holds a failed summary with no tail, and 1.18.0's an output
-- pruned after the compaction. Written by hand; no row of a real
-- database.
